archiso v87 copies only /boot/vmlinuz-* and /boot/initramfs-*.img from the
airootfs into the ISO (_make_boot_on_iso9660), then empties /boot. A unified
kernel image built by the profile's customize_airootfs.sh -- here the arm64
live UKI carrying the Windows-on-ARM device trees, configs/aarch64/live-uki.sh
-- never reaches the ISO. Copy /boot/*.efi next to the kernel so a GRUB entry
can chainload it. ISO 9660 only: the El Torito FAT image keeps the plain
kernel and initramfs, which the fallback entry boots. Applied by
builder/build-iso.sh to the vendored submodule copy on aarch64 builds only.

Retire when: archiso ships UKIs from /boot itself (no upstream MR as of
2026-08-25; see JimmayVV/omarchy-iso#12 and #21).

--- a/archiso/mkarchiso
+++ b/archiso/mkarchiso
@@ -433 +433 @@ _make_boot_on_iso9660() {
-    local ucode_image
+    local ucode_image _uki
@@ -437,0 +438,6 @@ _make_boot_on_iso9660() {
+    # Unified kernel images built into /boot by the profile travel with the
+    # kernel they wrap, where a GRUB entry can chainload them.
+    for _uki in "${pacstrap_dir}/boot/"*.efi; do
+        [[ -e "${_uki}" ]] || continue
+        install -m 0644 -- "${_uki}" "${isofs_dir}/${install_dir}/boot/${arch}/"
+    done
